This code uses the `Object_Detector_Tool` class and the `detected_objects` variable as input. It creates a tuple containing a dictionary mapping each label to the detection results and a dictionary mapping each label to the total number of detected objects in the image. The `saved_image_path` parameter is set to an empty string in the demo commands, so the open_image decorator does not need to be called.

The `Pixel_Depth_Tool` class is not used here.
